What:           /sys/devices/platform/charging-policy/charge_control_limit
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        itskenny0 <0@kenny.cat>
Description:
                Battery charging current cap in microamps. Read/write, accepts
                500000 through 1000000 in 100000 increments. Initially 500000;
                Android restores its saved preference after persistent storage
                is ready. Automatic is a userspace choice mapped to 1000000.
                Zero is not Automatic. Policy may reduce or inhibit charging.
                This controls battery charge current, not total USB input draw.

What:           /sys/devices/platform/charging-policy/charge_start_level
What:           /sys/devices/platform/charging-policy/charge_stop_level
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        itskenny0 <0@kenny.cat>
Description:
                Charge level limit in percent of battery capacity, 0 through
                100. Read/write. Charging stops once the capacity reaches
                charge_stop_level and resumes once it falls to
                charge_start_level; in between the input keeps powering the
                system with charging inhibited (status reason level-limit).
                A start level at or above the stop level gives no hysteresis.
                charge_stop_level 100 (the default) disables the limit, as
                does an unavailable capacity reading. Written by the LineageOS
                health HAL's charging control "limit" mode.

What:           /sys/devices/platform/charging-policy/status
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        itskenny0 <0@kenny.cat>
Description:
                Read-only, coherent newline-separated key=value snapshot:
                requested_ua, applied_ua, input_ua, voltage_uv, measured_ua,
                reason, error. The applied fields are successfully commanded
                limits, not measured current. On error they are zero requests
                and MUST NOT be interpreted as proof of electrical isolation.
                measured_ua is the last sampled battery current, meaningful only
                with error=0. error is a negative errno or zero. Reasons are:
                waiting, unplugged, no-battery, sensor-error, charger-fault,
                safety-timer, temperature, voltage, usb-budget, user-limit,
                thermal-limit, ready, io-error, stale, stopped, level-limit.
                No battery capacity or health HAL is synthesized by this driver.
